 6. KEY FLOWS
 ────────────

  a) Authenticated API call
     client ─▶ nginx /api ─▶ ApiKeyMiddleware ─▶ handler
       ─▶ get_user_id_from_request ─▶ rbac::require_permission (DB lookup)
       ─▶ begin_as_user (RLS) ─▶ query ─▶ JSON

  b) Chat message (end-to-end encrypted)
     browser: encrypt for every participant key → WAYVE_CHAT_E2E_V1 envelope
       ─▶ WSS /ws/chat ─▶ websocket.rs rejects plaintext
       ─▶ AES-GCM storage layer ─▶ messages
       ─▶ Redis PUBLISH ─▶ every API instance ─▶ recipients' sockets
       ─▶ recipient browser decrypts locally
     reconnect: heartbeat + since_id resync

  c) Mailbox connect + sync (Gmail / Outlook)
     POST /api/email-providers/{p}/connect ─▶ consent URL (state stored)
       ─▶ provider ─▶ /oauth/{…}/callback ─▶ exchange code
       ─▶ tokens sealed into email_accounts (+ token_expiry)
       ─▶ initial sync spawned
     then: sync worker every 30s / Gmail push ─▶ reuse access token until
           <5 min left, else refresh ─▶ headers into emails
           ─▶ body worker fills bodies + attachments

  d) 1-on-1 call
     /ws/call signaling relay (RBAC scope gate) ─▶ SDP/ICE exchange
       ─▶ peer-to-peer media, Cloudflare TURN when NAT blocks

  e) Service access with an API key
     X-API-KEY ─▶ hash lookup ─▶ scope for (method, path) ─▶ rate limit
       ─▶ audit row ─▶ acts as the key's designated user_id everywhere


